+## Budgets
+
+```console
+$ tally budget set groceries 300
+set budget for 'groceries' to 300.00
+$ tally budget status --month 2026-03
+CATEGORY       LIMIT    SPENT  REMAINING    USED  STATUS
+eating-out   $100.00  $125.00    -$25.00  125.0%  over
+groceries    $300.00  $240.00     $60.00   80.0%  warning
+rent        $1200.00    $0.00   $1200.00    0.0%  ok
+---------------------------------------------------------
+total       $1600.00  $365.00   $1235.00   22.8%
+```
+
+`spent` counts only expenses (not income) dated within the month. A budget
+is `over` when spending exceeds its limit and `warning` when spending
+reaches `budget.warn_percent` % of it; otherwise `ok`.
+
+Budgets live in `budgets.txt`, one `category|limit` line each after a
+`# tally budgets v1` header, escaped like the ledger and written just as
+safely.
+
